exports[`flow generation prompt > with spec title and description, several endpoints 1`] = `
"You are helping build a multi-step intake wizard flow from an OpenAPI spec.

Below is a raw, mechanically-extracted list of write-operation endpoints, as JSON. There are exactly 3 endpoint(s), with these ids: createAccount, createVerification, createPayoutMethod. Each endpoint already has its final set of fields.

Rules:
1. The output "flow.endpoints" array must contain exactly these 3 endpoint(s) -- one object per input endpoint, each appearing exactly once, identified by its exact "id". Never split, duplicate, merge, or add an endpoint.
2. For each endpoint, "fields" must reference exactly that endpoint's own field names below (in any order you like) -- one entry per field, never a name from a different endpoint, never an invented one, never a missing one.
3. You may reorder the endpoints array into the most sensible sequence for a user filling out a multi-step wizard.
4. Write a clear, human-friendly "title" and "description" for the overall flow, and for each endpoint.
5. For each field, optionally set "labelOverride" and/or "descriptionOverride" to rewrite its label/description into clear, user-facing text -- this is most of the value you add, so do it for every field where the raw text could be clearer. Set either to null to keep the field's original label/description. (Field "type", "required", "enumValues", and "validation" aren't part of this output -- they're taken directly from the raw data below, so don't repeat them.)
6. List any field whose purpose or expected value is genuinely ambiguous from the spec alone in "ambiguousFields", with a short "note" explaining why -- do not change the field itself to address the ambiguity, just flag it for human review.

Spec title: Payment Onboarding API
Spec description: Accounts, verifications and payout methods.

Raw endpoints (JSON):
[
  {
    "id": "createAccount",
    "title": "POST /accounts",
    "description": "Creates an account.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "email",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Email",
        "required": true,
        "validation": {
          "pattern": "^[^@\\\\s]+@[^@\\\\s]+$"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "accountType",
        "type": "enum",
        "label": "Account Type",
        "required": true,
        "enumValues": [
          "individual",
          "business"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "address.city",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Address City",
        "description": "City of the mailing address.",
        "required": false
      }
    ],
    "auth": {
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "bearer"
    },
    "capabilities": {
      "read": true,
      "update": true,
      "undo": true
    },
    "resourcePath": "/accounts",
    "idParam": "accountId"
  },
  {
    "id": "createVerification",
    "title": "POST /accounts/{accountId}/verifications",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "dateOfBirth",
        "type": "date",
        "label": "Date of Birth",
        "required": false
      },
      {
        "name": "legalBusinessName",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Legal Business Name",
        "required": false
      }
    ],
    "auth": {
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "bearer"
    },
    "pathParams": [
      "accountId"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "createPayoutMethod",
    "title": "Add Payout Method",
    "description": "Bank account for payouts.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "bankName",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Bank Name",
        "required": true
      },
      {
        "name": "accountHolderName",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Account Holder Name",
        "required": true
      }
    ],
    "auth": {
      "type": "none"
    }
  }
]"
`;

