    "id": "createAccount",
    "title": "POST /accounts",
    "description": "Creates an account.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "email",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Email",
        "required": true,
        "validation": {
          "pattern": "^[^@\\\\s]+@[^@\\\\s]+$"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "accountType",
        "type": "enum",
        "label": "Account Type",
        "required": true,
        "enumValues": [
          "individual",
          "business"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "address.city",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Address City",
        "description": "City of the mailing address.",
        "required": false
      }
    ],
    "auth": {
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "bearer"
    },
    "capabilities": {
      "read": true,
      "update": true,
      "undo": true
    },
    "resourcePath": "/accounts",
    "idParam": "accountId"
  },
  {
    "id": "createPayoutMethod",
    "title": "Add Payout Method",
    "description": "Bank account for payouts.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "bankName",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Bank Name",
        "required": true
      },
      {
        "name": "accountHolderName",
        "type": "string",
        "label": "Account Holder Name",
        "required": true
      }
    ],
    "auth": {
      "type": "none"
    }
  }
]"
`;

exports[`invalidation prompt with guidance > full global and flow guidance 1`] = `
"In a multi-step intake wizard, the user went back and changed a step they had already completed. Decide which of the LATER completed steps may no longer be correct because of that change.

Guidance from the author of this form. Follow it where it applies, unless it conflicts with the other instructions in this prompt, which always take precedence:
<<<AUTHOR_GUIDANCE
Business context: Onboarding for sellers who want to receive payouts.
Tone: Friendly, concise, second person.
Write all user-facing text in: es-MX
Rules for this call:
- Accept P.O. boxes as valid addresses.
- Never ask for a middle name.
About this form: Most sellers are small businesses in Latin America.
AUTHOR_GUIDANCE>>>

Edited step: "POST /accounts" (createAccount)
Description: Creates an account.

Values before the edit (JSON):
{
  "accountType": "individual"
}

Values after the edit (JSON):
{
  "accountType": "business"
}

Later completed steps, with what was submitted for each (JSON):
[
  {
    "id": "createVerification",
    "title": "POST /accounts/{accountId}/verifications",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "dateOfBirth",
        "label": "Date of Birth"
      },
      {
        "name": "legalBusinessName",
        "label": "Legal Business Name"
      }
    ],
    "submittedData": {}
  },
  {
    "id": "createPayoutMethod",
    "title": "Add Payout Method",
    "description": "Bank account for payouts.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "bankName",
        "label": "Bank Name"
      },
      {
        "name": "accountHolderName",
        "label": "Account Holder Name"
      }
    ],
    "submittedData": {}
  }
]

Task: list in "affected" only the later steps whose submitted data, or whose set of relevant fields, plausibly depends on what changed (for example a name that must match, or fields that only apply to one account type). For each, give its exact "id" as "endpointId" and a short, user-facing "reason": one sentence, under 160 characters. Return an empty list if the change doesn't affect any later step."
`;

